{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>When a person commits a trespass against YHWH.</b> Here He has again written the section of one who robs and swears falsely — the same spoken of in the section of Vayikra: ״וּמָעֲלָה מַעַל בַּה׳ וְכִחֵשׁ בַעֲמִיתוֹ״ and so on. And it is repeated here for two things newly introduced in it: the first, that it writes ״וְהִתְוַדּוּ״ — teaching that he is not liable to the fifth and the guilt-offering on the testimony of witnesses until he himself confesses to the matter; and the second, concerning the robbery of a convert — that it is given to the priests (see Sifrei)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:26.766217594Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}